        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.
        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by performance issues related to the use of inefficient data structures (Set<String>) for storing words and stop words in the `KeepWordFilterFactory` and `StopFilterFactory`. This led to slower lookups and processing times, particularly when handling large sets of words. The patch replaces these with `CharArraySet`, which is optimized for performance in token filtering scenarios.

        Commit message:
        SOLR-1095: fix stopword and keep filter performance issue

git-svn-id: https://svn.apache.org/repos/asf/lucene/solr/trunk@761036 13f79535-47bb-0310-9956-ffa450edef68  

        Patch:
         import org.apache.lucene.analysis.StopAnalyzer;
 import org.apache.lucene.analysis.TokenStream;
+import org.apache.lucene.analysis.CharArraySet;

 import java.util.HashSet;

   public void inform(ResourceLoader loader) {
     String stopWordFiles = args.get("words");
     ignoreCase = getBoolean("ignoreCase",false);
